<BaseLayout
  title="EXP-003 · Offline Airflow Deployment | Airflow Lab"
  description="Mindmap and deployment workflow for running Apache Airflow on a Windows machine without Internet access."
>
  <article class="article">
    <div class="breadcrumbs">AIRFLOW LAB / EXPERIMENTS / EXP-003</div>
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:16px">Deployment / Air-Gapped Windows</div>
    <h1>Apache Airflow Offline Deployment</h1>
    <p>
      A practical deployment map for a Windows host with no Internet access. The recommended
      pattern is to prepare Docker images and Python dependencies on a connected machine,
      transfer them as artifacts, then run Airflow locally with Docker Compose.
    </p>

    <h2>01 · Deployment mindmap</h2>
    <pre><code>AIRFLOW OFFLINE DEPLOYMENT
│
├── 1. PLAN
│   ├── Define Airflow version
│   ├── Define execution environment
│   │   └── Windows + Docker Desktop + WSL2
│   ├── Define workload dependencies
│   │   ├── Python / pandas
│   │   ├── DB2 drivers
│   │   ├── MSSQL drivers
│   │   └── Internal SQL / ML packages
│   └── Define offline transfer method
│       └── USB / internal file share
│
├── 2. PREPARE ON INTERNET MACHINE
│   ├── Get docker-compose.yaml
│   ├── Pull all Docker images
│   │   └── docker compose pull
│   ├── Build custom Airflow image when needed
│   │   └── pandas / pymssql / pyodbc / DB2 tooling
│   ├── Prepare .env
│   │   └── AIRFLOW_UID + FERNET key
│   ├── Prepare DAGs
│   └── Prepare Python runtime
│       └── conda-pack for env_mortgage
│
├── 3. EXPORT ARTIFACTS
│   ├── docker compose config --images
│   ├── docker save
│   │   └── airflow-images.tar
│   ├── Export Conda environment
│   │   └── env_mortgage.tar.gz
│   ├── Copy source
│   │   ├── dags/
│   │   ├── plugins/
│   │   ├── config/
│   │   └── agent/ / jobs/
│   └── Create offline bundle
│       └── airflow-offline-bundle.zip
│
├── 4. TRANSFER TO OFFLINE MACHINE
│   ├── Copy bundle
│   ├── Verify file checksum
│   ├── Install / verify Docker Desktop
│   ├── Verify WSL2
│   └── Verify internal network to DB2 / MSSQL
│
├── 5. INSTALL OFFLINE
│   ├── Extract bundle to D:\airflow
│   ├── docker load -i airflow-images.tar
│   ├── Restore Python environment
│   ├── Configure .env
│   ├── docker compose up airflow-init
│   └── docker compose up -d
│
├── 6. VERIFY
│   ├── docker compose ps
│   ├── Airflow UI
│   │   └── http://localhost:8080
│   ├── Check DAG parsing
│   │   ├── airflow dags list
│   │   └── airflow dags list-import-errors
│   ├── Run test DAG
│   └── Test DB2 → MSSQL connectivity
│
├── 7. OPERATE
│   ├── Store DAGs under dags/
│   ├── Store execution code in Windows runtime
│   ├── Airflow Connections
│   │   ├── DB2
│   │   └── MSSQL
│   ├── Use Variables / Secrets safely
│   └── Monitor logs and task states
│
├── 8. BACKUP
│   ├── DAG source
│   ├── plugins/
│   ├── config/
│   ├── .env / keys securely
│   └── PostgreSQL metadata
│       ├── DAG state
│       ├── Task instances
│       ├── Connections
│       └── Variables
│
└── 9. NETWORK PATTERN
    ├── Preferred
    │   └── Airflow → Windows Agent → env_mortgage
    └── Fallback
        └── Windows Agent polling / outbound-only pattern</code></pre>

    <h2>02 · Recommended architecture</h2>
    <pre><code>                 CONNECTED MACHINE
                         │
        ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
        │                │                │
        ▼                ▼                ▼
   Docker images      DAG source      Python env
   airflow*.tar       dags/           conda-pack
        │                │                │
        └────────────────┼────────────────┘
                         │
                  USB / internal share
                         │
                         ▼
                ┌────────────────────┐
                │   OFFLINE WINDOWS  │
                │                    │
                │ Docker Desktop     │
                │ ┌────────────────┐ │
                │ │ Airflow        │ │
                │ │ Scheduler      │ │
                │ │ DAG Processor  │ │
                │ │ Worker/API     │ │
                │ └───────┬────────┘ │
                │         │          │
                │ Windows Agent      │
                │   env_mortgage     │
                └───────┬────────────┘
                        │
                 Internal network
                  ┌─────┴─────┐
                  ▼           ▼
                 DB2        MSSQL</code></pre>

    <h2>03 · Connected machine: export checklist</h2>
    <pre><code># 1) Pull images
docker compose pull

# 2) Inspect exact image list
docker compose config --images

# 3) Export images
docker save -o airflow-images.tar &lt;image1&gt; &lt;image2&gt; &lt;image3&gt;

# 4) Package Python execution environment
conda pack -n env_mortgage -o env_mortgage.tar.gz

# 5) Bundle source/config
docker-compose.yaml
.env
dags/
plugins/
config/
agent/
jobs/</code></pre>

    <h2>04 · Offline machine: import and start</h2>
    <pre><code># Load images
docker load -i airflow-images.tar

# Verify
docker images
docker compose config --images

# Initialize metadata DB
docker compose up airflow-init

# Start stack
docker compose up -d

# Verify health
docker compose ps</code></pre>

    <h2>05 · DAG validation</h2>
    <pre><code>docker compose exec airflow-dag-processor airflow dags list

docker compose exec airflow-dag-processor airflow dags list-import-errors

docker compose exec airflow-dag-processor   ls -la /opt/airflow/dags</code></pre>

    <h2>06 · Dependency strategy</h2>
    <p>
      Do not depend on <code>pip install</code> from the offline host. For Airflow dependencies,
      build a custom image on the connected machine and transfer that image. For Windows-only
      execution dependencies, package the Conda environment separately and restore it on the
      offline host.
    </p>

    <div class="two">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Airflow image</h3>
        <p>
          Orchestration dependencies, providers, shared Python libraries and any packages that
          must exist inside Airflow containers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Windows runtime</h3>
        <p>
          DB2/MSSQL drivers, pandas-heavy ETL, model libraries and business code that must run
          in <code>env_mortgage</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>07 · DB2 → MSSQL execution path</h2>
    <pre><code>Airflow DAG
    │
    ▼
Windows Agent / local task launcher
    │
    ▼
env_mortgage
    │
    ├── Extract from DB2
    │
    ├── Transform / validate
    │
    └── Load to MSSQL
              │
              ▼
         Data Mart / Feature Store</code></pre>

    <h2>08 · Production notes for an offline bank environment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep image versions pinned so the offline environment is reproducible.</li>
      <li>Never put database passwords directly inside DAG source; use Airflow Connections or an approved secret mechanism.</li>
      <li>Keep an inventory of Docker images, package versions, drivers and checksums in the offline bundle.</li>
      <li>Test the full path on a non-production offline host before promotion.</li>
      <li>Back up the Airflow metadata database in addition to DAG source code.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      Outcome: the offline host needs no Internet at runtime. Internet access is required only on the
      preparation machine used to obtain and package images, providers, Python environments and source.
    </div>
